items.body:
Cookie corruption bug in error response handling. When `getSetCookie()` is not available, this fallback uses `headers.get('set-cookie')` which returns a comma-concatenated string of all Set-Cookie headers. Since Set-Cookie headers can contain commas in Expires dates, this will corrupt multi-cookie responses.

```typescript
// Bug: This corrupts cookies when multiple Set-Cookie headers exist
if (!sourceCookies.getSetCookie && source.headers.has('set-cookie')) 
  headers.append('set-cookie', source.headers.get('set-cookie')!);

// Fix: Iterate through entries to preserve individual cookies
if (!sourceCookies.getSetCookie) {
  for (const [key, value] of source.headers.entries()) {
    if (key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie') {
      headers.append('set-cookie', value);
    }
  }
}
```

This will break authentication flows in browsers that don't support `getSetCookie()`, causing session cookies to be malformed and rejected.
```suggestion

    if (!sourceCookies.getSetCookie) {
      for (const [key, value] of source.headers.entries()) {
        if (key.toLowerCase() === 'set-cookie') {
          headers.append('set-cookie', value);
        }
      }
    }

```


